  Description: Description
  ReferanceDescription: Single target tower with a long range. Focuses on one enemy
    until it dies or leaves the tower's range.
  RealLifeEquivalentDescription: The Brazil nut tree is one of the longest-lived
    residents of the Amazon, often reaching 500 to 1,000 years of age. Its massive,
    woody fruit pods can take over a year to mature and are heavy enough to be fatal
    if they fall on someone below. It was a mystery how anything could pierce these
    rock-hard shells until it was discovered that the Agouti, a large rodent, is
    the only animal with the specialized teeth needed to crack them open.
